### Collection for the REST Client extension (VS Code) or the IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Examples use the data in database.sql (user 1, PAMP = instrument 47, ARS = instrument 66).
### Same examples: Swagger UI (http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html) and postman/cocos-api.postman_collection.json.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### Portfolio of user 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/portfolio/1

### Search assets by ticker or name (case-insensitive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/instruments?query=pamp

### List all assets
GET {{baseUrl}}/instruments

### MARKET buy by exact quantity (executes at the latest close -> FILLED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 47,
  "side": "BUY",
  "type": "MARKET",
  "size": 10
}

### MARKET buy by amount in pesos (size = floor(amount / close))
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 47,
  "side": "BUY",
  "type": "MARKET",
  "amount": 10000
}

### LIMIT buy (stays NEW and reserves size * price from the available cash)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 47,
  "side": "BUY",
  "type": "LIMIT",
  "size": 5,
  "price": 900.50
}

### MARKET sell (REJECTED if it exceeds the available shares)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 47,
  "side": "SELL",
  "type": "MARKET",
  "size": 5
}

### Incoming peso transfer
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 66,
  "side": "CASH_IN",
  "type": "MARKET",
  "amount": 50000
}

### Outgoing peso transfer (REJECTED if it exceeds the available cash)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 66,
  "side": "CASH_OUT",
  "type": "MARKET",
  "amount": 10000
}

### Cancel a NEW order (seed order 5 is a pending LIMIT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/5/cancel

### Cancel a FILLED order -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/2/cancel

### Invalid request (LIMIT without price) -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "instrumentId": 47,
  "side": "BUY",
  "type": "LIMIT",
  "size": 1
}
